  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2026-08-12T12:37:08.505Z",
  "deleteID": null,
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "https://feedback.vrchat.com/open-beta/p/1881-its-indistinguishable-if-a-user-is-friend-or-not-in-recently-seen-page was fixed improperly. One important feature that was lost is the ability to see the order of recently seen people regardless of whether they are friends or not.\n\n \n\nThe previous UI allowed me to find people based on their avatars or other people I remember seeing, regardless of whether they were friends or non-friends.\n\nIn my personal opinion, the previous UI in build 1881, where it was indistinguishable whether a user was a friend or not, was better than the current separated lists. People may have different opinions on this, though.\n\nI think it would be better to add a friend icon to each user, similar to the user search results page, instead of separating friends and non-friends into different lists.",
